# IFOS live medium package list
#
# Design rule: the ISO stays small. Heavy end-user applications (browsers,
# games, IDEs, office suites) are NOT shipped here - they are offered by
# `ifos-software`, which installs them on demand in the live session and on the
# installed system. Nothing was dropped from the distro, only moved behind an
# installer. See airootfs/usr/share/ifos/apps.d/.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Base system (upstream archiso releng set - keep in sync when rebasing)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
base
linux
linux-headers
linux-firmware
linux-firmware-marvell
linux-atm
amd-ucode
intel-ucode
mkinitcpio
mkinitcpio-archiso
mkinitcpio-nfs-utils
sudo
diffutils
less
man-db
man-pages
nano
vim
rsync
pv
screen
tmux
mc
squashfs-tools
xdg-utils
zsh
grml-zsh-config

# Terminfo for terminals that may connect to the live system
foot-terminfo
ghostty-terminfo
kitty-terminfo
kmscon-terminfo
rxvt-unicode-terminfo
terminus-font

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Storage, partitioning and filesystems
#   These are what make the installer able to actually format a disk.
#   setup_ifos2.sh had deleted this entire block, which is why installing failed.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
parted
gptfdisk
fatresize
dosfstools
e2fsprogs
btrfs-progs
xfsprogs
f2fs-tools
exfatprogs
ntfsprogs
jfsutils
nilfs-utils
udftools
bcachefs-tools
mtools
lvm2
mdadm
dmraid
cryptsetup
open-iscsi
nbd
lsscsi
sdparm
sg3_utils
hdparm
smartmontools
nvme-cli
mmc-utils
usbutils
usb_modeswitch
usbmuxd
libusb-compat
bolt
dmidecode
# lspci. Three things read it and all three fail quietly without it: the
# installer's graphics menu, which is what decides whether any GPU driver gets
# installed at all; the installer's check for a Broadcom wireless chip, which
# is what decides whether that laptop has Wi-Fi after the reboot; and
# ifos-gpu, which is how the launcher knows to run games on the dedicated card.
# It was arriving only as somebody else's dependency, which is not a guarantee.
pciutils
# glxinfo. `ifos-gpu --check` asks it one question - what is actually drawing -
# and that answer is the difference between "the driver is installed" and "the
# driver is working". A machine rendering on the CPU looks entirely normal
# until something asks for a game, so without this the doctor can list missing
# packages but cannot tell whether the graphics are broken.
mesa-utils

# Rescue / recovery tooling
clonezilla
partclone
partimage
fsarchiver
ddrescue
gpart
testdisk

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Networking
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
networkmanager
network-manager-applet
nm-connection-editor
wpa_supplicant
iwd
iw
wireless_tools
wireless-regdb
b43-fwcutter
broadcom-wl
modemmanager
dhcpcd
systemd-resolvconf
bind
ldns
ndisc6
dnsmasq
darkhttpd
nfs-utils
openssh
openvpn
openconnect
vpnc
ppp
pptpclient
xl2tpd
wvdial
ethtool
tcpdump
nmap
lftp
irssi
lynx

# Smartcards / security tokens
pcsclite
libfido2
openpgp-card-tools
sequoia-sq
tpm2-tools
tpm2-tss

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Boot / firmware
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
grub
efibootmgr
edk2-shell
refind
syslinux
memtest86+
memtest86+-efi
os-prober
plymouth

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Virtual machine guest support
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
hyperv
open-vm-tools
qemu-guest-agent
virtualbox-guest-utils-nox

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Accessibility (the boot menu advertises a speech option - keep it working)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
brltty
espeakup

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Installation tooling
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
arch-install-scripts
archinstall
reflector
dialog
gparted
git

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Xorg + i3 desktop
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
xorg-server
xorg-xinit
xorg-xrandr
xorg-xsetroot
# The i3 config runs `xset s 600` and `xset dpms 0 0 720` at login. Without
# this package that line simply fails, and the two things it was there to do -
# blank the screen after ten minutes, and hand xss-lock its cue to lock - never
# happen. A school laptop then sits unlocked with the backlight on until the
# battery gives out, which is the opposite of both intentions.
xorg-xset
# The X input driver. It is only an optional dependency of xorg-server, so it
# was arriving by chance as something else's dependency - and nothing that
# 30-touchpad.conf configures applies without it being the driver in use.
xf86-input-libinput
xterm
xfce4-terminal
i3-wm
i3lock
xss-lock
libnotify
thunar-volman
thunar-archive-plugin
polybar
rofi
picom
dunst
feh
alacritty
thunar
gvfs
# Removable media. thunar-volman only acts while Thunar is open - it is a
# Thunar plugin - so on the plain desktop a pendrive did nothing at all when
# plugged in: no mount, no notification, nothing to click. udiskie mounts it
# and says so, which on a school machine is most of what storage means.
udisks2
udiskie
tumbler
xarchiver
mousepad
maim
xclip
xdotool
arandr
# Plugging a projector in did nothing at all: X sees the output, i3 does not
# configure it, and the second screen stayed dark. autorandr ships the udev
# rule and the systemd user unit that notice a display change, and its built-in
# "horizontal" profile lays out whatever it finds side by side - so an unknown
# projector in an unfamiliar room works without anyone having saved a profile
# for it first.
autorandr
# Warms the screen after sunset. Coordinates are pinned to Dourados in
# /etc/skel, so this needs no geolocation service and works offline.
gammastep
htop
# A task manager you can read without knowing htop's keys: process list, and
# CPU / memory / network graphs. GTK, so the IFOS theme already covers it, and
# small enough not to be a joke on the hardware this runs on.
xfce4-taskmanager
fastfetch
fish
bash-completion
unzip
zip
7zip
xdg-user-dirs

# IFOS launcher (full-screen front end, embedded Moodle view)
webkit2gtk-4.1
adwaita-icon-theme
adwaita-cursors

# Session management / privileges
sddm
# sddm-greeter links against Qt5, not qt6-declarative. Without this the ifos
# login theme's `import QtQuick.Controls 2.15` fails to resolve and SDDM
# silently falls back to its bundled default theme.
qt5-quickcontrols2
polkit
polkit-gnome

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Audio
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
pipewire
pipewire-pulse
pipewire-alsa
wireplumber
alsa-utils
livecd-sounds
sof-firmware
pavucontrol
pamixer
playerctl
brightnessctl

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Power and memory
#   Both of these exist for the same reason: the machines this runs on are old.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Power profiles, switchable from the bar. Deliberately not tlp: the two
# conflict, and tlp has no equivalent of a profile you can change from the
# desktop without a root shell.
power-profiles-daemon
# Compressed swap in RAM, configured in /etc/systemd/zram-generator.conf.
# Swapping to a mechanical disk is what makes an old machine unusable rather
# than merely slow.
zram-generator

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Bluetooth
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
bluez
bluez-utils
blueman

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Fonts and theming
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ttf-jetbrains-mono-nerd
noto-fonts
noto-fonts-emoji
otf-font-awesome
adw-gtk-theme
papirus-icon-theme
qt5ct
qt6ct
kvantum
xsettingsd
python-gobject
